<.page title="Proxy" description="How Edge Admin provides HTTP and SOCKS5 access through the secure mesh.">
  <article class="guide-content guide-topic">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">← Guide overview</a>
    <p class="kicker">Capability</p><h1>Proxy is a general network capability.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Edge Admin exposes HTTP and SOCKS5 forward proxies so clients can reach network targets through the secure mesh.</p>
    <section><h2>More than an SSH tunnel</h2><p>SOCKS5 carries any TCP connection, not only SSH. Use it for HTTP clients, database tools, internal services, and protocols that have no dedicated Edge Admin feature. The HTTP proxy handles HTTP traffic; SOCKS5 is the general TCP option.</p><p>You can route directly to a VPN node or chain through a chosen agent to reach the internet or LAN from that agent's network location.</p></section>
    <section><h2>The access boundary stays centralized</h2><p>Clients authenticate to the proxy endpoint, while the mesh and Edge Admin decide how traffic reaches the target. This avoids exposing each managed machine's ports publicly just to make a connection possible.</p></section>
    <section class="next"><h2>Use it</h2><p>Configure your HTTP client or SOCKS5-capable tool with the Admin proxy endpoint and proxy key. Then select the direct or chained route that fits the target.</p><div class="next__links"><a class="primary-link" href="/guide/ssh">How SSH uses proxy <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/swaggerui#/Ssh.SshUsername">SSH credential API</a></div></section>
  </article>
</.page>
